From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:36:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 476/488] [DS4.1] Sink: the alternates' rows in one TileLang
 launch; the policy writes the recovered zeros

alternate_logprobs_of computed each request's drawing row, gathered the rows
and clamped every alternate with torch, then scored the alternates one at a
time and copied each score into its column. sink_rows copies the rows densely
and clamps the alternates in one launch (with a logits logprobs mode, it also
takes their logits); one log-softmax launch scores every alternate of a row
(the row's maximum and log-sum-exp do not depend on how many tokens are
scored), and the rank kernel ranks one alternate a launch into its row of
alternate-major ranks. The rank and log-softmax kernels are unchanged.

The policy reads the step's alternate logprobs and ranks at their strides,
and in its logprobs variant writes every request's recovered logprob and rank,
0 where nothing was recovered, so apply no longer zero-fills them.

The sink declares the copy for each logits dtype and the log-softmax of the
dense rows; the runner passes the logprobs mode.
